um packaging products for the beverage, personal care, and household products industries in the United States, Brazil, and internationally. The company manufactures and sells aluminum beverage containers to fillers of carbonated soft drinks, beer, energy drinks, and other beverages. It manufactures and sells extruded aluminum aerosol containers, recloseable aluminum bottles, aluminum cups, and aluminum slugs. The company was founded in 1880 and is headquartered in Westminster, Colorado.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Ronald J. Lewis | CEO & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $2.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 16K people. Revenue per employee of $823K ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $49K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Ball Corporation is a large-cap consumer cyclical business with a $17.0B market cap on $13.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -5% over the past three years and +5% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, and 16% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $788M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.38\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 4.4\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 9.0% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 16% margin of safety against estimated fair value","40 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is Ball (BALL) Undervalued Following Its Quarterly Loss Or Already Priced For Recovery?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/materials/nyse-ball/ball/news/is-ball-ball-undervalued-following-its-quarterly-loss-or-alr","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794554458.147,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.71,"ti